---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../lib/site';
---
{currentSite(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_KEY) === 'agdr' ? <Layout title="Specification"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">AgDR 1.2.0 · Published</p><h1>Agent Decision Record Specification.</h1><p class="lede">The normative specification defines the file location, required frontmatter, status values, decision body and validation rules for consequential technical decisions made by agents.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Normative source.</strong><br /><a href="/agdr-spec.md">Read the published SPEC.md</a> · <a href="https://github.com/me2resh/agent-decision-record/blob/main/SPEC.md">View source repository</a>.</div><h2>What AgDR records</h2><p>An AgDR records what an agent decided, the context that led to the decision, and the rationale that should remain available after the session ends.</p><h2>JSON serialisation</h2><p>JSON is an additional serialisation of the AgDR information model. Markdown stays the repository-native representation. The two representations MUST preserve the same decision semantics. See <a href="/agdr-spec.md#9-json-serialisation">section 9 of SPEC.md</a> and the <a href="/schema/agdr-json.schema.json">JSON Schema</a>.</p><h2>Interoperability</h2><p>Typed relationships may be added as an extension. They are informative until adopted by the AgDR specification.</p></section></Layout> : <Layout title="Specification"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT v0.1 · Draft</p><h1>Planning and Reconciliation Specification.</h1><p class="lede">An ORBIT Plan is a portable declaration of durable software intent and outcomes designed to be reconciled against current reality before execution work is materialised.</p><div class="callout"><strong>A Plan is not a backlog.</strong><br />ORBIT keeps intent durable while deriving only the next bounded execution slice from current reality.</div><h2>Conventions</h2><p>The key words MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT and MAY express normative requirements in this draft.</p><h2>Artefacts</h2><p>A Plan MUST contain durable intent, outcomes and acceptance criteria. A Project Snapshot records repository state at a point in time. A Reconciliation compares the two and records observations, assessments and evidence. An Execution Slice describes one bounded software change and its provenance.</p><h2>Revision and staleness</h2><p>A Plan revision changes when durable intent or planning knowledge changes. Repository revisions belong to snapshots and reconciliations. An executor MUST block a slice when a relevant repository commit differs from the slice provenance.</p><h2>Execution neutrality</h2><p>ORBIT does not define coding agents, issue trackers, branch workflows, CI/CD, model providers, source-control hosting, or orchestration systems.</p><p><a href="/schemas">View the draft schemas</a> · <a href="/concepts">Read the concepts</a></p></section></Layout>}
